FALL-AIRGAP
===========

The 6-byte Primorial-Fold codec at the heart of this transport is the Konomi
architecture, created by Thomas Frumkin, and is used here with permission.

The signature-first gate (verify-before-parse), the opcode and resource sets,
the κ-witness fold, and the zero-budget phantom honeypot are reused from
SENTINEL (https://github.com/sjgant80-hub/sentinel), vendored verbatim as
sentinel.mjs. SENTINEL's kernel is mutation-gated in its own repository.

This repository (fall-airgap) adds the transport layer — event encoders,
the wire framing, the byte-ratio measurement, delta/coordinate streaming,
the Human Door, and the tiered reroute policy — and measures the compression
claim in real wire bytes.

